%% Secure N-Tier - Observability Architecture (replaces CloudWatch-only view)
%% Rendered natively by GitHub. Source of truth for diagrams/README.md #11.
flowchart TB
    Users --> R53[Route 53 DNS]
    R53 --> WAF[AWS WAF v2]
    WAF --> ALB[ALB public subnets]
    ALB --> TG[Target Group HTTP/HTTPS]
    TG --> ASG1[ASG AZ-a: EC2 + Docker<br/>backend:3000 /metrics<br/>frontend:80]
    TG --> ASG2[ASG AZ-b: EC2 + Docker<br/>backend:3000 /metrics<br/>frontend:80]
    ASG1 --> RDS[(RDS MySQL Multi-AZ)]
    ASG2 --> RDS

    subgraph CloudWatch path - AWS native
      ALB --> CW[CloudWatch Metrics]
      ASG1 --> CW
      RDS --> CW
      CW --> AL[CloudWatch Alarms x9]
      AL --> SNS[SNS Topic]
      SNS --> Email[ops email]
      CW --> CWD[CloudWatch Dashboard]
    end

    subgraph Self-hosted observability - NEW
      ASG1 -. scrape /metrics .-> PROM[Prometheus :9090]
      ASG2 -. scrape /metrics .-> PROM
      NE[node-exporter :9100<br/>cAdvisor :8080] --> PROM
      BB[blackbox :9115<br/>probe frontend/health<br/>backend:3000/health] --> PROM
      PROM --> GRAF[Grafana :3001<br/>dashboards + alerts]
      DOCKER[Docker logs] --> PT[Promtail]
      PT --> LOKI[Loki :3100]
      LOKI --> GRAF
      GRAF --> SNS
    end

    S3[(S3 state + ALB logs)] -.-> CW
    SM[Secrets Manager] -.-> ASG1
    SM -.-> ASG2
